MedGemma.description:
This cluster is likely enriched with FoxP3+ regulatory T cells, consistent with the high FoxP3 expression. The presence of CD4 and CD20 suggests a T cell population, potentially a subset of regulatory T cells. The low expression of DNA1, Pancytokeratin, and TTF1 is suggestive of a non-epithelial cell type. The co-expression of CD3 and CD8a could indicate a T cell population with a mixed phenotype, possibly including CD8+ regulatory T cells. The overall profile is consistent with a population of regulatory T cells, potentially involved in immune suppression or maintaining immune homeostasis within the tumor microenvironment."}
